/*
  The words of the diagram bank, by slide number.

  The diagrams themselves are the teacher's slides (diagram-bank.json) and are
  kept exactly as drawn. Their titles, though, were whole sentences, some run
  together without a space ("... from P to P2Consumer surplus ..."), some so long
  they were cut off with "..." in a list. So each slide has:

    title    a short name, 60 characters at most, for lists and headings
    caption  one or two complete sentences saying what the diagram shows, shown
             under the drawing and used to word the revision question

  A slide with no entry keeps the teacher's wording.

  HIDDEN: market-specific copies of a simple idea (a coffee market showing the
  same shift as the generic one) are left out of the bank and of diagram
  revision. They stay in the data because essay plans and other screens look
  diagrams up by number.
*/
