  127: { title: 'Long-run equilibrium with normal profit only', caption: 'In the long run the price line MR = AR touches the lowest point of AC, where MC cuts AC at output Q. Price equals average cost (P = C), so only normal profit is earned and firms have no incentive to enter or leave.' },
